  "steps": [
    "Soften the onions and pepper in oil over medium heat for 10 minutes until sweet.",
    "Stir in the garlic and all the spices and cook for a minute until the kitchen smells incredible.",
    "Add the beans, tomatoes and stock, bring to a simmer and cook uncovered for 30 minutes, stirring now and then.",
    "Grate in the dark chocolate and stir until melted — it rounds out the smokiness.",
    "Finish with lime juice and salt to taste. Serve with rice, jacket potatoes or scooped up with tortilla chips."
  ],
  "notes": "The chocolate is the secret — it adds depth, not sweetness. This thickens as it sits, so loosen with a splash of water when reheating."
}
